ull,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.beta (3b48b0110)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta (3b48b0110) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n@HolonProduction \n\nApparently the caching of the script in the MRP does not work correctly. For example when using `Ctrl+Shift+F` to `Find in Files` and clicking on a match from the `gd` file the following errors are thrown, even though the file is already open (when changing the code mentioned here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109345#discussion_r2637928880 the error is not rethrown):\n<img width=\"905\" height=\"135\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/552aeceb-1f25-415f-a83f-4c20550dae3f\" />\n Interestingly this only happens on every 2nd click, could be related to the behavior described in the second paragraph of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111641\n> For some reason, clicking the line if script editor is not visible, will not jump to that line. You have to click again. ...\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- In the MRP press `Ctrl+Shift+F` to open `Find in Files`\n- Search for something in the example script (like `error`)\n- Click on `Find`\n- Click on the result (the errors should show up on every second click)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[close-tab-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24280660/close-tab-error.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-m